<!DOCTYPE html>
<html xmlns:o='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office' xmlns:w='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40'>
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>React.js Core & Component Patterns Revision</title>
<style>
  body { font-family: Calibri, 'Segoe UI', Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.5; color: #1e293b; margin: 30px; }
  h1 { font-size: 20pt; color: #0284c7; border-bottom: 2px solid #0284c7; padding-bottom: 6px; }
  h2 { font-size: 14pt; color: #0369a1; margin-top: 20px; border-bottom: 1px solid #cbd5e1; padding-bottom: 4px; }
  h3 { font-size: 12pt; color: #0f172a; margin-top: 14px; }
  p, li { margin: 4px 0; }
  .callout { background: #f0f9ff; border-left: 4px solid #0284c7; padding: 10px 14px; margin: 12px 0; border-radius: 4px; }
  .code { font-family: Consolas, 'Courier New', monospace; background: #f1f5f9; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 3px; font-size: 10pt; color: #0f172a; }
  pre { background: #0f172a; color: #38bdf8; font-family: Consolas, monospace; padding: 12px; border-radius: 6px; font-size: 10pt; overflow-x: auto; }
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 12px 0; }
  th, td { border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; padding: 8px 12px; text-align: left; }
  th { background: #f8fafc; font-weight: bold; color: #1e293b; }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<h1>⚛️ React.js Core Concepts & Machine Coding - Revision Notes</h1>
<div class="callout">
  <strong>Part 2 Master Revision Guide:</strong> React Elements, Components, JSX Transpilation, State vs Props, Key prop, Reconciliation, Controlled/Uncontrolled Forms, and UI Blueprints.
</div>

<h2>1. React Core Constructs</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>React Element:</strong> An immutable plain JavaScript object describing UI. Created via JSX or <span class="code">React.createElement()</span>.</li>
  <li><strong>React Component:</strong> A JavaScript function or class that returns React Elements and encapsulates logic.</li>
  <li><strong>React Node:</strong> Anything that can be rendered (elements, strings, numbers, arrays, null).</li>
</ul>

<h3>JSX Transpilation</h3>
<p>Browsers do not understand JSX directly. Babel transpiles JSX into <span class="code">React.createElement()</span> calls before execution.</p>

<h2>2. State vs Props & Immutability</h2>
<table>
  <tr>
    <th>Property</th>
    <th>State</th>
    <th>Props</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Origin</strong></td>
    <td>Managed internally inside the component</td>
    <td>Passed down from parent component</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Mutability</strong></td>
    <td>Mutable via setter (<span class="code">useState</span>)</td>
    <td>Read-only (immutable for child)</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Re-render</strong></td>
    <td>Updates trigger component re-render</td>
    <td>Changes trigger re-render of child</td>
  </tr>
</table>

<div class="callout">
  <strong>Immutability Golden Rule:</strong> Never mutate state directly (e.g., <span class="code">arr.push()</span>). Always create a new copy (<span class="code">[...arr, newItem]</span>) so React's shallow comparison detects reference change and re-renders properly!
</div>

<h2>3. Lists & The Key Prop</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Purpose:</strong> Keys help React's <em>Reconciliation (Diffing Algorithm)</em> uniquely identify which list elements changed, were added, or were removed.</li>
  <li><strong>Why Array Index as Key is Bad:</strong> Reordering or deleting list items causes index mismatch, leading to unnecessary re-renders and wrong UI state bugs in inputs. Use unique IDs!</li>
</ul>

<h2>4. Controlled vs Uncontrolled Components</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Controlled:</strong> Input value is managed by React state (<span class="code">value={state}</span> + <span class="code">onChange</span>). Single source of truth.</li>
  <li><strong>Uncontrolled:</strong> Input value is stored directly in the DOM. Accessed using <span class="code">useRef</span> on submission.</li>
</ul>

<h2>5. Machine Coding: Star Rating Component</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>States:</strong> <span class="code">rating</span> (saved) & <span class="code">hoverRating</span> (preview).</li>
  <li><strong>Formula:</strong> <span class="code">const isFilled = starValue &lt;= (hoverRating || rating);</span></li>
  <li><strong>Accessibility:</strong> Include <span class="code">role="button"</span>, <span class="code">tabIndex={0}</span>, and handle <span class="code">Enter</span>/<span class="code">Space</span> in <span class="code">onKeyDown</span>.</li>
</ul>

</body>
